# npm Project — Node.js build and review workflow
#
# This example shows:
#   - Typical JS/TS build pipeline
#   - Using the LLM for code review
#   - Chaining build -> test -> deploy
#
# Try it:
#   makethlm --list              # see available tasks
#   makethlm --dry-run build     # preview what would happen
#   makethlm check               # lint + review in one task

project := "my-app"

llm claude [model=sonnet]

# Install dependencies
task setup:
    !npm install

# Build the project
task build: setup:
    !npm run build
    !echo "Built {{project}} successfully."

# Run tests and analyze results
task test: build:
    !npm test 2>&1 || true
    Look at the test output above.
    If all tests passed, say "All tests passed."
    If any failed, explain the failures clearly
    and suggest specific fixes with code snippets.

# LLM-powered code review of recent changes
task review:
    !git diff --stat
    !git diff
    Review the git diff above for:
    - Bugs or logic errors
    - Security issues (XSS, injection, etc.)
    - Missing error handling
    - Style or readability problems
    Be concise and actionable. Skip nitpicks.

# Quick health check: lint + type check + review
task check:
    !npx eslint src/ 2>&1 || true
    !npx tsc --noEmit 2>&1 || true
    Look at the linting and type-check output above.
    Summarize the issues found, grouped by severity.
    Suggest the top 3 most important fixes.
